plan:   device-cache-mb 13020      [measured] the experts used most live on the processor that computes them fastest, as the RAM cache holds what flash would read: Vulkan0 computes this model's experts at 419 GiB/s against the host's 64, both measured on this model's own expert block; the 13020 MiB the fitter gave 7 of 43 layers' experts serve 16% of a token's routed bytes as a cache (the fraction of the expert set it holds); a miss is uploaded from the host
plan:   ubatch         0          [derived] a graph as wide as the context reserves 80 MiB of compute buffers, inside 10% of the 87618 MiB this process may hold: a prompt is computed in one pass
